ss":"many gems","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கு","parts":[{"text":"கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"heap (first part)"}],"gloss":"heap (first part)","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வையடும்","parts":[{"text":"வையடும்","lemma":"வையடும்","gloss":"with the heap"}],"gloss":"with the heap","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"விரைஇக்","parts":[{"text":"விரைஇ","lemma":"விரைஇ","gloss":"having mixed"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"க்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"having mixed"},{"surface":"`கொண்ம்`","parts":[{"text":"`கொண்ம்`","lemma":"`கொண்ம்`","gloss":"take!"}],"gloss":"take!","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எனச்","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"saying"},{"text":"ச்","lemma":"ச்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சுரத்துஇடை","parts":[{"text":"சுரத்துஇடை","lemma":"சுரத்துஇடை","gloss":"in the desert path"}],"gloss":"in the desert path","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நல்கி","parts":[{"text":"நல்கி","lemma":"நல்கு","gloss":"having given"}],"gloss":"having given"},{"surface":"யோனே","parts":[{"text":"யோனே","lemma":"யோனே","gloss":"he indeed"}],"gloss":"he indeed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"விடர்ச்","parts":[{"text":"விடர்","lemma":"விடர்","gloss":"mountain cleft"},{"text":"ச்","lemma":"ச்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"mountain cleft"},{"surface":"சிமை","parts":[{"text":"சிமை","lemma":"சிமை","gloss":"peak"}],"gloss":"peak"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓங்குஇருங்","parts":[{"text":"ஓங்குஇருங்","lemma":"ஓங்குஇருங்","gloss":"lofty and dark"}],"gloss":"lofty and dark","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொல்லிப்","parts":[{"text":"கொல்லி","lemma":"கொல்லி","gloss":"Kolli hills"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"ப்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"Kolli hills"},{"surface":"பொருநன்","parts":[{"text":"பொருநன்","lemma":"பொருநன்","gloss":"lord"}],"gloss":"lord"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓம்பா","parts":[{"text":"ஓம்பா","lemma":"ஓம்பு","gloss":"unstinting"}],"gloss":"unstinting"},{"surface":"ஈகை","parts":[{"text":"ஈகை","lemma":"ஈகை","gloss":"generosity"}],"gloss":"generosity"},{"surface":"விறல்வெய்","parts":[{"text":"விறல்","lemma":"விறல்","gloss":"victory"},{"text":"வெய்","lemma":"வெய்","gloss":"desiring"}],"gloss":"desiring victory"},{"surface":"யோனே","parts":[{"text":"யோனே","lemma":"யோனே","gloss":"he indeed"}],"gloss":"he indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"An arrow of excellent release that felled an elephant / caused death to a wide-mouthed tiger, / rolled over a hollow-horned spotted buck, / felled a mortar-headed wild boar, and in the nearby / deep anthill, struck a monitor lizard, / he who sat having made victorious his strong-bow hunt, / his arrow greatly playing with fame-filled excellence, / who indeed is this killer? This killer, / does not look like a seller of meat, he possesses wealth abundantly, / on his chest where a garland hangs down, / the lord of the fruitful mountain with waterfalls on the slopes, / is he Ori? Or is he not? / I will sing, O songstress, one melody, and you / prepare the clay-tuned drum, tune the lute, / play the flute with open holes like the breath of a male elephant, / play the small drum, play the akuli drum, / play the one-headed drum gently, / give the supporting staff to my right hand, saying / since he is the lord, we approached him speaking, / and having performed the twenty-one themes according to the rules, / at the time when we named him 'King', there / since it was his own name, he felt shy, and we said, / 'We come from country to country, here / there are no hunters equal to you', / even as we spoke what we desired, he did not let us go, and from his hunt / having given toddy like melted cow's ghee, along with the fat boiled meat of the deer he killed himself, / and fine gold born of his mountain / mixed with a heap of many gems, saying 'Take!', / he gave it in the desert path, / the lord of the lofty, dark Kolli hills with mountain clefts and peaks, / he who desires victory with unstinting generosity.","translation":"With a single arrow shot from his strong bow, he felled an elephant, brought death to a wide-mouthed tiger, rolled over a hollow-horned spotted buck, brought down a mortar-headed wild boar, and struck a monitor lizard inside a deep anthill nearby. Sitting victorious after his hunt, his arrow playing with fame-filled excellence, who indeed is this hunter? He does not look like a seller of meat; he possesses abundant wealth. On his broad chest hangs a garland, and he is the lord of the fruitful mountain with waterfalls on its slopes. Is he Ori, or is he not?\n'I will sing, O songstress, a melody, and you prepare the clay-tuned drum, tune the lute, play the flute that sounds like the breath of a male elephant, play the small drum, play the akuli drum, play the one-headed drum gently, and place the supporting staff in my right hand,' saying thus, since he is the lord, we approached him. Having performed the twenty-one themes of song according to the rules, when we addressed him as 'King', he felt shy because it was his own name. We said, 'We travel from country to country, and there are no hunters here equal to you.'\nEven as we spoke our desires, he did not let us go. He gave us toddy as clear as melted cow's ghee, along with the fat boiled meat of the deer he had killed himself in the hunt. He mixed fine gold born of his mountain with a heap of many gems, and saying 'Take!', he bestowed them upon us right in the desert path. He is the lord of the lofty, dark Kolli hills with its clefts and peaks, a victorious hero of unstinting generosity.","modern":"வலிய வில்லால் எய்த ஒரு அம்பினால் யானையை வீழ்த்தி, பெரிய வாயையுடைய புலியை இறக்கச் செய்து, துளையுள்ள கொம்புகளையுடைய புள்ளிகளுள்ள கலைமானை உருட்டி, உரல் போன்ற தலையையுடைய காட்டுப் பன்றியை வீழ்த்தி, அருகில் இருந்த ஆழமான புற்றிலிருந்த உடும்பையும் கொன்று, வேட்டையை வெற்றிகரமாக முடித்து அமர்ந்திருந்தான் ஒருவன். அவனது அம்பு மிகுந்த புகழுடன் விளங்கியது. இந்தக் கொலைத்தொழில் செய்பவன் யார்? இவன் இறைச்சியை விற்கும் வேடன் போலத் தெரியவில்லை; மிகுந்த செல்வம் உடையவனாகத் தோன்றுகிறான். மார்பில் மாலை அணிந்தவன்; அருவிகள் பாயும் மலைக்குத் தலைவன். இவன் ஓரியா? அல்லது வேறு யாரா?\n'விறலியே! நான் ஒரு பண் பாடுவேன். நீ மண் பூசிய முழவை ஆயத்தம் செய்; யாழைத் தாளத்திற்கு நிறுத்து; யானையின் மூச்சுப் போல ஒலிக்கும் குழலை ஊது; எல்லரி மற்றும் ஆகுளிப் பறைகளை முழக்கு; பதலை என்னும் ஒருதலைப் பறையை மெல்ல இயக்கு; எனது வலக்கையில் ஊன்றுகோலைத் தா' என்று கூறி, அவன் தலைவன் என்பதால் அவனை அணுகிப் பாடினோம். இசையின் இருபத்தொரு துறைகளையும் முறைப்படி பாடி முடித்து, அவனை 'அரசே' என்று அழைத்தபோது, அது தன் பெயராக (ஓரி என்பதற்குத் தலைவன் என்றும் பொருள்) இருந்ததால் அவன் நாணமடைந்தான். 'நாங்கள் நாடெங்கும் சுற்றி வருபவர்கள்; உனக்கு இணையான வேடன் எங்கும் இல்லை' என்று கூறினோம்.\nநாங்கள் விரும்பியதைச் சொன்னபோதும் எங்களை உடனே போகவிடாமல் தடுத்தான். தான் வேட்டையாடிக் கொன்ற மானின் கொழுத்த இறைச்சியையும், பசு நெய் போன்ற தெளிந்த கள்ளையும் தந்து உபசரித்தான். தன் மலையில் பிறந்த மாசற்ற பொன்னையும், பல மணிக் குவியல்களையும் கலந்து 'பெற்றுக்கொள்' என்று கூறி, பாலை வழியிலேயே எங்களுக்குப் பரிசாக அளித்தான். அவன் பிளவுகளையும் சிகரங்களையும் கொண்ட உயர்ந்த கொல்லி மலையின் தலைவன்; வாரி வழங்கும் கொடையாளன்.","explanation":"This poem is in the Paatān tinai, composed by the poet Vanparanar in praise of the chieftain Valvil Ori. The poet describes an extraordinary feat of archery where a single arrow shot by Ori pierces through an elephant, a tiger, a deer, a wild boar, and a monitor lizard. Amazed by this skill, the poet and his troupe of musicians perform for the chieftain, addressing him as 'King' (Ko), which makes the modest ruler blush. Recognizing their talent, Ori treats them with great hospitality, serving them fresh venison and fine toddy, and rewards them lavishly with gold and gems right on their path. The poem beautifully illustrates the chieftain's dual qualities of unmatched valor in hunting and unstinting generosity in patronage.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}